; A macro whose template names something this module IMPORTED, for
; `595-macro-imported-ambiguous.ax`. `dup` resolves here to `AmbB`'s,
; and that is what the macro means wherever it is invoked; an entry
; file that imports `AmbA` as well makes the name ambiguous, and the
; rewrite refuses to choose. A second reader BOUND `dup` at the
; invocation until 2026-08-16, when that stopped being capture and
; became an ordinary reference to the macro's own scope - so this file
; names one fixture now, not two, and carries the ambiguity alone.
(import AmbB)

(pub macro (useDup v) (dup v))
